 "text": "We run on 100+ AI employees. Not 1 of them can send a refund on its own. Here's the rule, so you can copy it. Let AI draft anything. But 4 things always wait for a person's yes. Money going out. A message to a customer. A quote or a contract. Deleting data. Try this today. List every AI tool your team uses, and next to each one, write which of those 4 it can do alone. If it can do any of them, add a yes step. Anthropic's new assistant works the same way. It asks before it pays. In our live workshop, we'll set up your first AI employee with you, with the yes built in. Want in, comment workshop, and we'll send you the details. The next date's in our bio."
